# r1113 Power Grid boot on jar jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-15.jar (sha1 f95311cc26f8, port
# phase 9.3: all of -14 (P9b design table, schematic item, editor packets; fixes B20 to B24) plus P9c: acid fluid,
# etching, circuit assembly chains, battery assembly; fixes B25, B26). Supersedes pwg14.qb (-14 never booted).
# One boot, one batch, this order:
#   1. SQ-PWG-72 boot check, P9b part only (registries of P9b, menus, packets, zpwg9 / zpwg9b check, reload); the
#      version, phase, ns counts and recipe count moved to SQ-PWG-76 (the -15 boot row)
#   2. SQ-PWG-57 rerun for fix B20 (copy of pwg10b.qb's row; the -10 failure was
#      `held=ae2:wireless_terminal fe 0/3200000 -> 0/3200000 charge 20000/20000 -> 0/20000`)
#   3. P9b rows: SQ-PWG-73, -74, -75 (queue run order; CQ-PWG-24 / -25 are client rows, not here)
#   4. P9c rows: SQ-PWG-76 (version 19.2-15, phase 9.3, counts, 100 recipes, zpwg9c check, chain source board),
#      SETUP15, SQ-PWG-77 (acid), -78 to -81 (survival chain, in this order on this boot), -82 (B25), -83 (battery)
#      (CQ-PWG-26 is a client row, not here)
# Group A superflat, level pwg15, spawn-animals=true, ground Y -61 (grass), blocks at Y -60. Each area's SETUP row kills
# the animals generated in its chunks (box selector) and stops mob spawning.
# Areas (no block overlap):
#   P9b   X 1090 to 1130, Z 1805 to 1850 (SQ-PWG-72 forceload, kept; -73 Z 1810 to 1825, -74 / -75 Z 1820 to 1835)
#   P7    X 1095 to 1115, Z 1535 to 1545 (SETUP14P7; SQ-PWG-57's fake player at 1100 -60 1540, no blocks)
#   P9c   X 1135 to 1200, Z 1855 to 1915 (SQ-PWG-76 forceload; board 1140 1858; -77 flow 1183..1197 x 1859..1873,
#         bucket 1170 1862, pen 1175..1177 x 1879..1881; -78 Z 1865 to 1866; -79 Z 1873 to 1874 X 1142 to 1152;
#         -83 Z 1881 to 1882; -80 Z 1890; -81 Z 1898 to 1900; -82 Z 1905 to 1910; Create machines at Y -61 to -57)
# Prep (INST = the instance root; all before the boot):
#   COPYDEV=1 PGJAR=$INST/jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-15.jar prep_srv.sh OUT pwg15 A spawn-animals=true
#   ls OUT/srv/mods | grep -i -E 'powergrid|cc-tweaked'   (only backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-15.jar: remove -14 and
#     older; cc-tweaked-1.19.2-1.101.4.jar present); sha1sum of the jar starts f95311cc26f8
#   for p in pwg_probe pwg_grid_probe pwg_p3_probe pwg_p4_probe pwg_p5_probe pwg_p6_probe pwg_p7_probe pwg_p8_probe pwg_p9a_probe pwg_p9b_probe pwg_p9c_probe; do
#     cp $INST/tools/scratch_query/$p.js OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_$p.js; done      (eleven probes, the CURRENT copies;
#     p9b has the CircuitSchematicItem class check by instanceof; p9c has the r1113 Rhino fixes: absMoveTo, getEncodeId,
#     tick-count game time, RecipeApplier by signature, Create 0.5.1 DirectBeltInputBehaviour package)
#   ponder datapack from the -15 jar (77 structure files; SQ-PWG-72 checks it is enabled, no row places from it):
#   rm -rf OUT/pwgp; mkdir -p OUT/pwgp OUT/srv/pwg15/datapacks/pwgponder/data/pwgponder/structures \
#     && unzip -o -q OUT/srv/mods/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-15.jar 'assets/powergrid/ponder/*' -d OUT/pwgp \
#     && cp -r OUT/pwgp/assets/powergrid/ponder/. OUT/srv/pwg15/datapacks/pwgponder/data/pwgponder/structures/ \
#     && printf '{"pack":{"pack_format":10,"description":"PWG ponder structures, scratch only"}}' > OUT/srv/pwg15/datapacks/pwgponder/pack.mcmeta
#   find OUT/srv/pwg15/datapacks/pwgponder -name '*.nbt' | wc -l      (77)
#   Loading Protection (shorter protection window, as pwg10 / pwg12):
#   python3 $INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py toml OUT/srv/config/loadingprotection-common.toml '"Loading Protection Configuration"' protectionDuration 1
#   Nothing else: no CC program, no other datapack, no config edit (the P9b rows use /give-free probe slots and packets;
#   the P9c rows build their machines with zpwg9c: creative motors at 64 RPM, the belt motor at 32).
# Run: qrun.py run OUT tools/scratch_query/batches/r1113/pwg15.qb perf/runs/r1113/pwg15
# Probe goggle reads log a RuntimeDistCleaner ERROR (client class): no blanket ERROR reject.
# waitlog matches anywhere since the row start; real waits are sleeps (20 ticks = 1 s) plus pace (s after each command).
# Batch deviations from the row text: tick waits are sleeps (pace 1 s after each command); SQ-PWG-57 adds its own
# forceload (SETUP14P7) and, for B20, checks only that the held item gains FE and the charge falls (the -10 pattern
# 0 -> 0 with the charge emptied is rejected); the wireless terminal may take the whole 20000 in one tick, so the old
# `1\d{4}` charge bound is dropped (record FE gained = charge lost per tick); SQ-PWG-73's 100 V / 130 V reads use
# 1 s sleeps after the source change. P9c: bucket use on the server returns CONSUME (sidedSuccess), accepted beside
# SUCCESS; MCA replaces the summoned pen villager (type mca:*villager accepted, kill by box not by type); the hurt
# event fires per acid roll (also inside the hurt cooldown), so SQ-PWG-77 counts >= and records the rate; lineck runs
# twice (the second after 1 s, a no-op when the first saw east); SQ-PWG-82 adds a show of the full stone depot;
# SQ-PWG-83 does not branch: a byproduct ends the row LOOK (rerun it with --rows SQ-PWG-83).
pace 1

